          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb1a2544d5fac0e77f2ce4fd84de9b669df34c0ca580ab6c5c24df50624a3bba:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7d970ab3bf074f6d8ca5018ab2715d11",
      "statement": "Git and JobQueue are each registered as a singleton and then exposed as a hosted service via a factory resolving that same singleton, so the IHostedService and the injected collaborator are one instance rather than separate objects.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L22-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fee6b797141bf852590d80f4cd28e8c4a88741a28993832cdc533e698c3f3f89:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5a15d96c598d4b6eb709c22610b27b99",
      "statement": "Startup deliberately differs by collaborator: GitHubService and ProviderResolver are resolved eagerly right after the host is built so missing credentials or provider configuration fail startup, whereas the git startup sync is best-effort and bounded to ten seconds so a missed push webhook cannot prevent the app from starting.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L42-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c929e30b2209c342f3a1782e8af22f55dd8f0bbbdd57b6997d044e750f1f5eee:"
